2026-06-02 14:19:15,211 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: # 1. Executive Summary
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., along with its consortium partners EuroCloud Solutions S.A., LexIA GmbH, and GreenCompute S.r.l., is pleased to submit a proposal for the implementation of an artificial intelligence solution to assist the City of Belval's administrative services. Our team brings extensive experience in managing large-scale projects, including 23 public sector references, such as Comune di Torino, Regione Lombardia, and Métropole de Lyon. We are committed to delivering a high-quality AI-powered tool that enhances the efficiency and quality of service provided by the municipal agents.

# 2. Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval seeks an intelligent assistance tool for its administrative services, aiming to improve access to information, enhance answer quality, and reduce processing times. The solution must integrate with existing systems, ensure data protection and sovereignty, provide explicability and transparency, and comply with regulatory requirements such as GDPR.

# 3. Proposed Solution
To address the City of Belval's needs, we propose a comprehensive AI solution that leverages our expertise in LLMs (Large Language Models), RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) capabilities, and sovereign hosting options. Our preferred model is Mistral 7B Instruct, which offers strong French-language performance, EU origin, and self-hostable nature under the Apache 2.0 license.

Our solution will be built using Docker and Kubernetes for efficient deployment and scaling, ensuring a response time of less than 2 seconds as required. We will utilize Prometheus and Grafana for monitoring and optimizing system performance. The integration with existing systems, including business software and electronic document management, will be achieved through REST or GraphQL APIs.

For data protection and sovereignty, we adhere to strict GDPR compliance, hosting data exclusively within the EU, and utilizing anonymization tools such as Microsoft Presidio and custom NER models. Our AI security controls include prompt injection protection, output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, confidence threshold escalation, model isolation, and model update security review.

We will provide explanations for our solution's outputs through XAI methods like source citation, chain-of-thought display, SHAP for classification models, and LIME. Our past experience in deploying AI solutions for public administration demonstrates our capability to adapt to various regulatory environments and user needs.

Our project management approach is based on PRINCE2, Agile Scrum, and SAFe methodologies, ensuring effective governance and risk management. We have a dedicated project manager certified in PMP or PRINCE2 Practitioner, who will lead the project and maintain logs such as RAID, decision, and change request processes.

Our budget for this project is estimated based on our standard daily rates of 900-1,000 euros, with an overhead monthly cost of 145,000 euros. Given the global budget allocated to the project is 3 million euros over 4 years, we aim for a target gross margin percentage of 28%, which translates to approximately 840,000 euros. Our financial eligibility threshold matches the project's global budget, confirming our ability to manage this contract.

In terms of environmental sustainability, our partnership with green hosting providers OVHcloud and Scaleway, both using 100% renewable energy, aligns with the City of Belval's goal of reducing energetic consumption. We also apply digital sobriety practices such as INT8/INT4 model quantization to reduce GPU energy by approximately 40%, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching to reduce recomputes by around 20%, and a green IT hardware procurement policy with a minimum 5-year lifecycle.

# 4. Unaddressed Requirements
Upon reviewing the tender requirements and our agents' contributions, we have addressed all specified needs. However, we note that our current technology stack's specifics regarding meeting the less than 2-second response time requirement could be further detailed. Additionally, potential trade-offs between response time, availability, and other constraints might need consideration in the design of the technical architecture.

# 5. Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., along with its consortium partners, is well-equipped to deliver an AI solution that meets the City of Belval's requirements for improving administrative services' efficiency and quality. Our proposal integrates project management expertise, technical capabilities, security and compliance measures, legal adherence, budgetary management, innovation in AI, and commitment to CSR and sustainability. We believe our comprehensive approach positions us favorably to deliver a successful project that aligns with the City of Belval's digital transformation strategy and enhances its public services.
